PART 2 -- beta -> infinity / Gaussian action = the real acid point
==============================================================================
  Take S_W = (1/2) phi^T A phi with A = -Delta + m^2  (SPD), the free field of mass m.
  B_t(x) = int K_t(z) e^{-S_W(x+z)} dz  with K_t(z) = (2 pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-|z|^2/2t}
  =>  B_t prop exp(-(1/2) x^T (A - A M^{-1} A) x),  M = A + t^{-1} 1
  =>  Hess V_t = A - A(A + t^{-1})^{-1}A = A^{1/2}[1 - (1 + A^{-1}/t)^{-1}]A^{1/2} >= 0
      (spectrum: a - a^2/(a + 1/t) = a/(1+at) >= 0).  =>  q == 0  =>  Q(inf) = 0.
  This holds for EVERY Gaussian S_W, hence in particular at beta = infinity.

  witness lattice T^4_3 (n = 81), t-grid 33 log-spaced points in [0, 1e3]
       m min_t lambda_min(Hess V_t)   q=max(0,-lam_min)   Q(inf)=int q
    0.50         9.960159362550e-04           0.000e+00      0.000e+00
         (spectrum is EXACT: eig(Hess V_t) = a/(1+at); matrix-vs-spectral max err 6.08e-15)
         (COV-T's form A(I+2tA)^-1 at t=1e-3: min eig 2.499e-01)
    1.00         9.990009990010e-04           0.000e+00      0.000e+00
         (spectrum is EXACT: eig(Hess V_t) = a/(1+at); matrix-vs-spectral max err 8.44e-15)
         (COV-T's form A(I+2tA)^-1 at t=1e-3: min eig 9.980e-01)

  Now the free field's TRUE constant.  For the Gaussian measure N(0, C) with
  C = A^{-1} and E(f,f) = int |grad f|^2 d mu :  gamma = 1/lambda_max(C) = lambda_min(A).
  On a torus the k = 0 mode is present (periodic), so lambda_min(A) = m^2 exactly.

     L   lambda_min(A) (k=0)          m^2     |diff| lambda_min (k!=0) = m^2+4sin^2(pi/L)
