  [T] gamma_free(m) = m^2 .   BD at the free point gives gamma >= 0.75 (or 0.375).
  VIOLATION  <=>  m^2 < 0.75  <=>  m < 0.866025   (N/4 reading)
             <=>  m^2 < 0.375  <=>  m < 0.612372   (N/8 reading)
  At m = 0 (massless free field, a -> 0): gamma_free = 0 < 0.75 : the criterion's
  conclusion is FALSE.  And it is false at every FINITE m below the crossing --
  no limit is being taken.  That is the acid point, and the failure is pointwise.

