  So: lambda_1(free, finite L) > 0  is TRUE (the premise of death-line (b)), but it
  does NOT make the failure a limit-only statement: the quantitative bound is
  already violated at FINITE L and at FINITE m.  Table of the four readings above:
    L* = 3.704 / 8.173 / 8.173 / 16.656  ->  integer thresholds 4 / 9 / 9 / 17
    (R1's own normalisation, gamma <= 2 m_1, with c = N/4 and c = N/8, gives
     L* = 16.656 and 33.46 -> violated at L >= 17 and L >= 34).
  What IS limit-only is the *sign* statement: on any finite lattice every beta has
  a gap (finite volume, discrete spectrum), so no sign test can ever fail.
  => the acid test can only be about UNIFORMITY / the continuum limit, but the
     failure is already visible at finite parameters.  Both halves matter.

